<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # What is Artificial Intelligence? – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Intelligent Robots</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> What is Artificial Intelligence?</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
                    <b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Communication: Resolve misunderstandings in group projects. Communication: Aid in negotiating group roles.
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">
                    <b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can resolve misunderstandings about AI's impact on society by using simple terms and gestures to explain (e.g., uses hand motions to simulate learning and says, "AI is a technology that is programmed to learn from data and perform tasks like humans.")
                    Can help assign roles in group projects on AI, using visuals or quick sketches to illustrate roles based on classmates' interests (e.g., "Would you like to focus on AI in education or in the workplace?" with icons representing each sector).
                    Can clarify the group's goals for projects on AI's societal impacts, ensuring each role is understood with visual aids (e.g., "Our project will discuss how AI could change jobs and daily life," using a timeline of technology evolution for context).
                </p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 34%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher begins by projecting a challenging headline related to AI's impact, e.g., "Robots to Replace Half of All Jobs by 2030, Report Predicts." Students are asked to briefly share their initial reactions or interpretations of the headline. The teacher encourages students to think about how they would explain this headline to someone who doesn't understand technology well.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to simplify a complex statement from the headline, for example: "To replace half of all jobs by 2030" -> "AI might take over many jobs in the next few years." The teacher uses a hand gesture (e.g., sweeping motion) to indicate "many" and points to a hypothetical calendar for "next few years." The teacher models the pronunciation of /ɑː/ in "robot" and "job," and the alternation of full and reduced vowels in "innovative" /ˈɪn.ə.veɪ.tɪv/ and "technological" /ˌtek.nəˈlɒdʒ.ɪ.kəl/ while explaining. Students repeat words after the teacher.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Am I trying to make the headline sound more complicated or simpler?" (Expected answer: Simpler.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When would you need to explain something complex like AI's impact in simple terms?" (Expected answer: When talking to someone who doesn't know much about it, or explaining a project to the group.)</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Intelligent Robots".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short, authentic excerpt (e.g., 150-200 words) from a technology blog or an online article discussing the complex societal impacts of AI, specifically focusing on "Intelligent Robots" and their evolving functionality. The excerpt contains examples of conditional forms, future simple, and passive voice. It also uses vocabulary such as <i>algorithms, data, employment opportunities, societal challenges, revolutionize, enhance, personalize, integrate, predict.</i></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will be able to interpret and explain information about the advanced functionality of intelligent robots and their implications, preparing them to mediate discussions about complex AI concepts.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the main idea of this article about intelligent robots?" "According to the text, what are some key future predictions about AI?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students match complex statements from the text (e.g., "AI systems are increasingly programmed to develop sophisticated learning algorithms.") with simple summaries provided by the teacher (e.g., "AI software is getting smarter at learning.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Teacher-led discussion:</b> Teacher asks "How might AI change jobs in Panama?" to prompt sociolinguistic practice, and "AI brings new possibilities but also some challenges for the future, doesn't it?" to encourage sensitive discussion.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Mediation.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice resolving misunderstandings and clarifying complex AI concepts using conditional forms (e.g., "If AI continues to evolve, it might change the job market significantly."), future simple (e.g., "AI will create new employment opportunities."), and passive voice (e.g., "AI systems are programmed to learn from data and perform tasks."), along with target vocabulary (e.g., <i>society, opportunities, challenges, algorithms, evolve, revolutionize, adapt</i>).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled practice – "Simplify the Statement":</b> The teacher provides a list of 5-6 complex sentences related to AI's impact (from the previous reading or new ones), using target grammar structures. Students work individually to rewrite each sentence in simpler terms, aiming for clarity and using gestures or simple visuals in their mind. E.g., "If AI is integrated into customer service, human interaction will be drastically minimized." Student rewrites: "AI will make talking to people less common in customer service." (Teacher circulates and provides immediate feedback on accuracy and simplicity.)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled practice – "Explaining the Project Section":</b> Students are divided into small groups for their "AI Future Predictions Report" project. The teacher provides a specific, complex section title or requirement for the report (e.g., "Analyzing the socio-economic implications of advanced AI algorithms on global employment opportunities"). Each student takes a turn explaining this section title to their group members in simple terms, using at least one conditional form, one future simple sentence, and a gesture or quick sketch on a mini-whiteboard/paper. Group members listen and suggest simpler words if needed.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair interaction – "Role Clarification Dialogue":</b> In their project groups, students pair up. One student describes a potential role for the "AI Future Predictions Report" project (e.g., "You will be responsible for researching the ethical guidelines for AI development."). The other student asks for clarification using phrases like, "What exactly does 'ethical guidelines' mean?" or "If I do that, what will I need to prepare?". The first student then mediates by explaining the role and terms using simpler language and offering a visual (e.g., drawing a balance scale for ethics or a magnifying glass for research). They switch roles.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Intelligent Robots".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Collaborative Group Mediation Session.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in their established project groups for the "AI Future Predictions Report." Their task is to hold a "Mediation Session" where they finalize their project roles and outline the main sections of their report, ensuring everyone understands their responsibilities and the project's goals. One student in each group acts as a designated mediator for the first part of the session, whose primary role is to ensure clear communication and resolve any misunderstandings. This role can rotate.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group is provided with a "Project Task Card" outlining the overall requirements for the "AI Future Predictions Report" (e.g., covering 'AI's impact on job markets,' 'ethical considerations,' and 'future technological advancements').</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The mediator facilitates the discussion, asking each member about their interest in specific report sections (e.g., "Would you like to focus on AI in education or in the workplace?" with quick sketches of a classroom or office).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">When a group member expresses confusion or a misunderstanding about a role or a report section, the mediator must step in to clarify using simpler language, gestures (e.g., hand motions to simulate "learning from data"), or visual aids (e.g., drawing a quick diagram of data flow for "algorithms").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students use target grammar: "If you choose this role, you will be responsible for collecting data on employment opportunities." "The report will be structured into three main parts." "AI systems are developed to enhance human capabilities." They also use pragmatic language like, "How will AI change the job market?" and sociolinguistic sensitivity: "AI brings new possibilities but also some challenges for the future."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The goal is for each group to have a clear understanding of who is doing what for the "AI Future Predictions Report" and what each section entails, documenting their decisions.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Assessment.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their group's documented "Project Roles and Section Outline" for the "AI Future Predictions Report," along with a brief written summary by each student explaining their assigned role and how it contributes to the overall project, emphasizing how misunderstandings were resolved or roles clarified.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and Simplicity:</b> Ability to explain complex AI concepts and project roles using simple, understandable terms and gestures.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Language:</b> Appropriate and accurate use of conditional forms, future simple, passive voice, and target vocabulary related to AI.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration and Resolution:</b> Effective participation in mediating group discussions, resolving misunderstandings, and negotiating roles collaboratively.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible Pronunciation:</b> Clear pronunciation of key vocabulary and multisyllabic words, including /ɑː/ and reduced vowels.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one challenging concept about AI you had to explain simply today, and how did you do it?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did using gestures or visuals help you or your group understand project roles better?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Reflecting on our 'AI Future Predictions Report' project, what was the most effective way you mediated a misunderstanding or clarified a role for a classmate?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How will the skill of explaining complex ideas simply help you in future academic or professional situations?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What strategies for teaching mediation (e.g., visual aids, specific phrases for clarification) worked well today? Were students able to apply the grammatical structures (conditionals, future simple, passive voice) effectively in their mediation efforts? What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for students to further develop their mediation skills in the context of academic projects, especially those involving complex technological themes?</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This lesson concludes the "What is Artificial Intelligence?" theme. The next lesson will transition to a new theme, applying the 21st-century skills of critical thinking and collaborative problem-solving developed here, potentially by having students present their finalized "AI Future Predictions Report" or engage in a debate on a related topic using their refined understanding of AI concepts.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>